Urology</italic></source><year>2003</year><volume>170</volume><issue>4</issue><fpage>1213</fpage><lpage>1216</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14501727</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B9"><label>9</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kotkin</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Brock</surname><given-names>JW</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Isolated ureteral injury caused by blunt trauma</article-title><source><italic>Urology</italic></source><year>1996</year><volume>47</volume><issue>1</issue><fpage>111</fpage><lpage>113</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8560642</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B10"><label>10</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Boone</surname><given-names>TB</given-names></name><name><surname>Gilling</surname><given-names>PJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Husmann</surname><given-names>DA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Ureteropelvic junction disruption following blunt abdominal trauma</article-title><source><italic>Journal of Urology</italic></source><year>1993</year><volume>150</volume><issue>1</issue><fpage>33</fpage><lpage>36</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8510270</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B11"><label>11</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Nicolaisen</surname><given-names>GS</given-names></name><name><surname>McAninch</surname><given-names>JW</given-names></name><name><surname>Marshall</surname><given-names>GA</given-names></name><name><surname>Bluth</surname><given-names>RF</given-names></name><name><surname>Carroll</surname><given-names>PR</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Renal trauma: re-evaluation of the indications for radiographic assessment</article-title><source><italic>Journal of Urology</italic></source><year>1985</year><volume>133</volume><issue>2</issue><fpage>183</fpage><lpage>187</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">3968728</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B12"><label>12</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lynch</surname><given-names>TH</given-names></name><name><surname>Mart&#x000ed;nez-Pi&#x000f1;eiro</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Plas</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>EAU guidelines on urological trauma</article-title><source><italic>European Urology</italic></source><year>2005</year><volume>47</volume><issue>1</issue><fpage>1</fpage><lpage>15</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15582243</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B13"><label>13</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hardeman</surname><given-names>SW</given-names></name><name><surname>Husmann</surname><given-names>DA</given-names></name><name><surname>Chinn</surname><given-names>HKW</given-names></name><name><surname>Peters</surname><given-names>PC</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Blunt urinary trauma: identifying those patients who require radiological diagnostic studies</article-title><source><italic>Journal of Urology</italic></source><year>1982</year><volume>128</volume><fpage>p. 456</fpage></element-citation></ref><ref id="B14"><label>14</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Powell</surname><given-names>MA</given-names></name><name><surname>Nicholas</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name><name><surname>Davis</surname><given-names>JW</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Blunt ureteropelvic junction disruption</article-title><source><italic>Journal of Trauma</italic></source><year>1999</year><volume>47</volume><issue>1</issue><fpage>186</fpage><lpage>188</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10421213</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B15"><label>15</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Best</surname><given-names>CD</given-names></name><name><surname>Petrone</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Buscarini</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Traumatic ureteral injuries: a single institution experience validating the american association for the surgery of trauma-organ injury scale grading scale</article-title><source><italic>Journal of Urology</italic></source><year>2005</year><volume>173</volume><issue>4</issue><fpage>1202</fpage><lpage>1205</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15758748</pub-id></element-citation></ref></ref-list></back><floats-group><fig id="fig1" position="float"><label>Figure 1</label><caption><p>CT scan showing urinoma, contrast extravasation (arrow) with a right pelvicaliceal dilatation.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="CRIM.UROLOGY2011-541705.001"/></fig><fig id="fig2" position="float"><label>Figure 2</label><caption><p>Retrograde ureteropyelogram showing opacification of all the upper urinary tract with extravasation of the contrast material in the ureteropelvic junction (arrow).</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="CRIM.UROLOGY2011-541705.002"/></fig><table-wrap id="tab1" position="float"><label>Table 1</label><caption><p>AAST organ injury severity scale for the ureter [<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="B15">15</xref>].</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead><tr><th align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Grade</th><th align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Description of injury</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">I</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Haematoma only</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">II</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Laceration &#x0003c;50% of circumference</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">III</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Laceration &#x0003e;50% of circumference</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">IV</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Complete tear &#x0003c;2 cm of devascularization</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">V</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Complete tear &#x0003e;2 cm of devascularization</td></tr></tbody></table></table-wrap></floats-group></article>